      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In December 1893, Swiss immigrant Sam Peterson renamed the post office from Kennedy to Engadine, echoing his homeland's valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        14,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/engadine_michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After logging declined, doctor William McNamara founded the Hiawatha Sportsman’s Club in 1927, preserving land for fishing and hunting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
